Subject: Cantor Phase3 Topology Scanner Exploded Specification

@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Scanner.sop

& [IdentityAxis] distinguishes names from physical objects
  + [path] is a canonical candidate-relative name
  + [strong_identity] is volume serial plus 128-bit file ID
  + [link_count] detects additional names
  + [scope] is one scan and never timeless identity

& [TraversalAxis] makes descent conditional
  + [enumerate] names a prospective child
  + [open_no_follow] obtains the terminal entry
  + [classify] records attributes, identity, links, and streams
  + [gate] admits ordinary directory descent only after every precondition passes
  + [repeat] detects intervening changes

& [AliasAxis] is uniformly rejecting
  + [symlink] is reparse
  + [junction] is reparse
  + [mount_point] is reparse
  + [other_reparse] is reparse
  + [hard_link] is link count not one
  + [same_object] is duplicate strong identity

& [StreamAxis] distinguishes absence from inability to observe
  + [unnamed_default] is ordinary file content
  + [named_data] is rejected
  + [no_streams] is valid only where platform semantics permit it
  + [unsupported] is an admission-denying platform fact
  + [error] preserves operation and OS code

& [RepositoryAxis] treats Git controls as interpretation authority
  + [candidate_content] excludes the admitted control boundary
  + [top_level_control] is fixed and separately digested
  + [nested_control] is rejected
  + [sparse_or_submodule] is rejected
  + [configuration_drift] is rejected

& [LimitAxis] bounds every multiplicative dimension
  + [breadth] is entry count
  + [depth] is directory depth
  + [name] is path bytes
  + [content] is per-file and aggregate bytes
  + [streams] is per-entry enumeration
  + [duration] is monotonic deadline

& [RaceAxis] states evidence strength honestly
  + [handle] stabilizes terminal-object queries
  + [pre_post] catches many object changes
  + [double_inventory] catches many tree changes
  + [gap] is not atomic snapshot
  + [response] is quarantine on observed or possible drift

& [AuthorityAxis] is five separately activated stages
  + [M2A] forms
  + [M2B] binding and unsafe review
  + [M2C] read-only implementation
  + [M2D] fixtures
  + [M2E] integration
  - never: infer a later authority from an earlier artifact
